{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535875-vampire-the-map-parade","id":1535875,"title":"Vampire: The Map-Parade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-18T17:01:55-07:00","id":1535875,"title":"Vampire: The Map-Parade","content":"I found line art of European-cities and thought, well, I can make these into a simple-map. I was reading V:tM core-book and well, here we are:<br /> <br /> I guess this is for some sort of alternate-history, or such. I used random name-generators for the names. I found black &amp; white English and European-countryside images, and used them to represent towns. This is circa 1900's. I even figured out the font used in the 2e book I was reading (Times New Roman) real original (but it's a standard-font). <br /> <br /> As for the Cainites, it's an overland map, meaning that, there's travel between the cites; I almost want, or can, make it Requiem with Invictus calling themselves the Camarilla. As per the 1760 report, the last Lupine was hunted off of the island. And despite being at the turn of the centuries, there are gangs of ruffians around, just like in a normal V:tM game. <br /> <br /> The biggest obstacle was finding and choosing line-art that matched, kinda, with the large-cities. I made several different versions before I settled; I used NBOS for the map-outline. <br /> <br /> (map is 3000x4000 pixels, two-color .gif)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://iili.io/JPSDTQt.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://iili.io/JPSDTQt.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <di